<title>FRANCE: UAP to report big 1996 loss -- paper.</title>
<headline>UAP to report big 1996 loss -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurer Union des Assurances de Paris (UAP) will post a 1996 loss of between six and seven billion francs as Axa, which took control of UAP in December, takes provisions to clean out its accounts, financial daily Les Echos reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The paper said Axa and major UAP shareholder Banque Nationale de Paris (BNP) would not have to consolidate the loss into their 1996 accounts because BNP stripped UAP from its accounts on January 1, 1996 and Axa will consolidate it from January 1, 1997.</p>
</text>
